From: Xiaomi Cepheus port
Subject: [PATCH] dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-cepheus: add local-bd-address for WCN3998 BT

WCN3998 (compatible "qcom,wcn3998-bt") sets HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY.
Without a "local-bd-address" property the controller is registered as
unconfigured: the hci_dev stays hidden from the BlueZ management interface
and "hciconfig hci0 up" fails with EOPNOTSUPP, so Bluetooth is unusable.

The BD address is already stored in the chip's NVM (crnv21.bin) and is what
Read BD_ADDR reports; declare the same address in DT so the driver programs
it during probe and the adapter comes up configured.

The address is stored LSB-first: bdaddr_t is filled as b[0..5] from the
property but displayed as b[5]:b[4]:b[3]:b[2]:b[1]:b[0], hence
[00 07 74 21 90 39] renders as 39:90:21:74:07:00.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-cepheus.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-cepheus.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-cepheus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-cepheus.dts
@@ -1094,6 +1094,7 @@

 	bluetooth: bluetooth {
 		compatible = "qcom,wcn3998-bt";
+		local-bd-address = [00 07 74 21 90 39];
 		vddio-supply = <&vreg_l1a_0p75>;
 		vddxo-supply = <&vreg_l7a_1p8>;
 		vddrf-supply = <&vreg_l2c_1p3>;
